Finding: this is the authoritative test the project has been building toward since
2026-08-31. jsmith authenticated to Entra ID with a password set moments earlier on DC01's
own AD, via Password Hash Sync over a UPN suffix (raytakosharkygmail.onmicrosoft.com) the
Entra Connect wizard displayed as "Not Added." The id matches the object already confirmed
exported (jsmith-exported-to-entra-id.json), and displayName/givenName/surname are now
populated from the synced AD attributes, not the bare stub breakglass's own /me call showed.
This resolves the practical question the "Not Added" status raised: whatever that label
means, it did not block a real user from signing in with their real on-prem credential.
It does not explain the root cause of the "Not Added" display itself — that remains a
separate, still-open cosmetic/UI question.
